  "notes": [
    "Dates are UTC: the link ran at 2026-10-05T01:41Z (seed_run.created_utc), which was 2026-10-04 in Pacific time. `captured_utc` is when this snapshot was read, not when the link ran.",
    "Run from a clean worktree at ce23db1 (origin/main) after `uv sync --locked`. The owner approved the --execute after reviewing the before_link checks. The models-root path is deliberately not recorded (public repo); it held the same staged copies as the 2026-10-04 candidate publish, and checks.before_link.staged_zips lists their hashes.",
    "`--promote` re-runs publish_card: log_artifact, then link_artifact(aliases=['production']). Each artifact's local manifest digest equalled registry v0 (checks.before_link.local_manifest_digest). wandb reported 'already exists with the same content. No new version will be created.' The read-back shows only v0 in each registry collection and each seed-project source sequence. Registry metadata already had the selectors shape, so publish_card's metadata-refresh save() branch was not taken.",
    "Lineage: because log_artifact was a no-op, run axw5245o lists the existing v0s as its logged artifacts, and their updated_at moved to 2026-10-05T01:41Z. logged_by() is still 4ihxu1mg, the candidate run that uploaded them. Nothing was re-uploaded.",
    "Per-version metadata is not repeated here. metadata_equals_card compares it with card_to_metadata(card) from the matrix at ce23db1. matrix_content_sha256 is unchanged from the 2026-10-04 record, so that record's metadata blobs still apply verbatim.",
    "`seed_run.rawconfig_only`: see the note in 2026-10-04-wheat-sorghum-candidate-publish-record.json; wandb lists wandb_version under run.rawconfig.",
    "`registry_state.before_link` equals the after-state of 2026-10-04-wheat-sorghum-candidate-publish-record.json.",
    "Rollback, if ever needed. (1) Unlink first. For each collection, fetch its `:production` link, assert is_link, and call unlink(); never save(). In wandb 0.28, unlink() sends UnlinkArtifactInput(artifact_id, artifact_portfolio_id), which removes the whole v0 membership. That removes `candidate` and `latest` as well as `production`, and the collection is left empty: keeping the cards on `candidate` would mean re-running the candidate publish. Ingested envelopes that reference these registry ids would stop resolving. (2) With a fresh wandb.Api(), check that `:production` is gone from all 3 and that predict list_cards() returns 8. (3) Only then re-pin the trait-extractor in talmolab/sleap-roots-pipeline to ghcr.io/talmolab/sleap-roots-trait-extractor:sha-426ad4d@sha256:7d5bdaf94dcaf1b695b0bfb2390bfb4dd687c0c18cb4720b25ce5bd43ed4b7e8 (the image that pipeline efb997e replaced with sha-e45b6bf). No traits image older than the deployed sha-e45b6bf has the wheat/sorghum rows, so never roll traits back while the cards are still linked."
  ]
